  "_exec_summary": [
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000123943,
      "SummaryText": "Accidental Release Prevention and Emergency Response Policies\nThe PRC-DeSoto International, Inc. Mojave, CA facility complies with applicable California and US EPA regulations and applicable Department of Transportation requirements.  PRC-DeSoto also follows the Responsible Care (registered service mark) Code of Management Practices, including the Responsible Care (registered service mark) Community Awareness Emergency Response (CAER).  PRC-DeSoto International is a wholly-owned subsidiary of PPG Industries, Inc. and follows PPG's own Community Awarenes and Emergency Response (CAER) Policy to assure emergency preparedness and foster community right-to-know.  PPG's CAER Policy requires each manufacturing plant to have a pro-active community awareness and emergency response program to handle emergencies that might happen in that facility.  All of these activities form an integral part of PPG's overall Environment, Health and Safety Policy, whose goal is \"to market, distribute, and manufacture products globally in a responsible manner that protect employees, neighbors, customers, and the environment.\"  \n\nRegulated Substances Handled\nPRC-DeSoto International Inc.'s Mojave, CA facility produces resins, adhesives and sealants used in the aerospace industry.  The facility stores and uses mixed isomers of Toluene 2, 4 Diisocyanate which is referred to as TDI.  The facility also stores and uses Formaldehyde (as 37% Formalin) and Propylene Oxide.  All of these compounds are listed in the US EPA's Risk Management Program.   The quantities of the above compounds that are stored and used at the Mojave, CA facility exceed the California Threshold Planning Quantities for the California Accidental Release Prevention (CalARP) Program.  In addition, the Mojave, CA facility also stores and uses Phenol, Isophorone Diisocyanate, Hydrofluoric Acid, and TDI-2,6 which are not subject to the Federal RMP, but are stored  in quantities which are above the California Threshold Planning Quantit"
    },
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 1,
      "FacilityID": 1000123943,
      "SummaryText": "ies under CalARP."
    }
  ]
}